  "answer": "In January 2023 Utah saw several senior‑living transactions. On January 9, 2023, a family office purchased a stand‑alone memory‑care community in Clinton (Ogden‑Clearfield area) that was built in 2016, has 66 beds across 45 units, and was being sold by a national owner/operator as a non‑core asset. Later, on January 26, 2023, 1031 Crowdfunding announced its first Utah acquisitions: the Spring Gardens communities in St. George and Lindon, built in 2011 and 2016 respectively, together providing 178 assisted‑living and memory‑care units and totaling 156,473 sq ft of space.",
